    "headline": "Furui is derived from the verb 旧る (furu, “to age”) plus し (-shi), an adjective-forming suffix.",
    "morphemes": [],
    "sources": [
      {
        "quote": "From Old Japanese. Attested in the Man'yōshū completed in 759."
      },
      {
        "quote": "In turn, derived from verb 旧(ふ)る (furu, “to age, to become older”, said of both things and people) + し (-shi, Old and Classical Japanese adjective-forming suffix), with the verb itself also attested in the Man'yōshū."
      },
      {
        "quote": "The modern form 古(ふる)い (furui) emerged as a regular shift from 古(ふる)き (furuki), the 連(れん)体(たい)形(けい) (rentaikei, “attributive form”) of classical adjective 古(ふる)し (furushi)."
      },
      {
        "quote": "⟨puruki₁⟩ → */puruki/ → /furui/"
      }
    ],
    "examples": [
      {
